{
  "id": "Lyo.Google.Geolocation.Client",
  "name": "Lyo.Google.Geolocation.Client",
  "area": "Integration",
  "tagline": "REST client for Google Maps plus an `IGeolocationService` implementation.",
  "description": "REST client for Google Maps plus an `IGeolocationService` implementation.\n\n**Archetype C.** Lives in `Integration/Google/` (vendor folder). Geolocation does not belong under Communication. The shape follows `Lyo.Endato.Client` plus a Core store, not `Lyo.Translation.Google`. Path is confirmed in [package layout](../../../docs/package-layout.md) (Phase 1).\n\nDepends on [`Lyo.Geolocation`](../../../Core/Geolocation/Lyo.Geolocation/README.md) and [`Lyo.Geolocation.Models`](../../../Core/Geolocation/Lyo.Geolocation.Models/README.md) only — not `Lyo.Geolocation.Postgres`. The host composes this client with the store.",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Host composition",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddPostgresGeolocationStoreFromConfiguration(configuration);\nservices.AddGoogleMapsClientFromConfiguration(configuration);\nservices.AddGoogleMapsGeolocationService();\n\n// Worker/API: geocode, then persist\nvar result = await geolocationService.GeocodeAsync(query, ct);\nawait geolocationStore.SaveAddressAsync(result.Address, ct);"
    }
  ],
